{
  "rules": [
    "If sentiment is consistently positive (≥0.67) over recent days, model tends to overestimate prices — reduce forecast slope or cap upward momentum.",
    "If sentiment is consistently negative (≤0.33) or mixed, model often underestimates — increase baseline or add downward bias correction.",
    "After a sharp price spike (forecast > 85.0), model frequently overcorrects with a steep upward trend — cap forecast growth to avoid overshoot.",
    "When true outcome shows strong mean reversion (e.g., 85.0+ → 75.0+), model often fails to adjust — apply downward bias if sentiment is neutral or negative.",
    "If forecast is rising steadily but true outcome shows early decline (e.g., 85.0 → 80.0 within 5 days), model is lagging — adjust for short-term volatility or sentiment-driven reversal.",
    "In sentiment-heavy periods (e.g., 1.00/0.00 alternation), model often misreads sentiment direction — align forecast slope with sentiment swing direction."
  ]
}
